---
import ShowcaseLayout from '../layouts/ShowcaseLayout.astro';
import InterfaceButton from '../components/ui/InterfaceButton.astro';
import FeatureCard from '../components/ui/FeatureCard.astro';
import FieldNoteCard from '../components/ui/FieldNoteCard.astro';
---

<ShowcaseLayout
	title="The operating structure behind trust."
	description="I help mission-driven teams turn complex digital work into clear decisions, trusted execution, and measurable momentum by designing the systems, signals, and stories that let strategy move."
	portraitSrc="/images/portrait-home.jpg"
	portraitAlt="Maggie Lynn"
>
	<!-- Hero CTAs -->
	<section class="content-panel">
		<div class="content-panel__content">
			<div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;">
				<InterfaceButton href="/work" variant="primary">View the Work</InterfaceButton>
				<InterfaceButton href="/frameworks" variant="secondary">Explore the Frameworks</InterfaceButton>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="content-panel__meta">
			<p>Current Focus<span class="content-panel__meta-value">Strategy-to-execution systems for mission-driven digital work</span></p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- The Thesis -->
	<div class="section-heading">
		<p class="section-heading__eyebrow">The Thesis</p>
		<div class="section-heading__line"></div>
	</div>
	<section class="content-panel content-panel--split">
		<header class="content-panel__header">
			<h2 class="content-panel__title">Strategy needs an operating layer.</h2>
		</header>
		<div class="content-panel__content">
			<p class="content-panel__body">Most complex work does not fail because people lack vision. It fails in the space between intent and execution, where priorities blur, decisions stall, risks stay invisible, and stakeholders lose the thread.</p>
			<p class="content-panel__body">That space is where I work: building the structures, rhythms, and narrative clarity that help teams understand what is happening, what matters now, and how to move next.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="content-panel__content">
			<p class="content-panel__eyebrow">01. Decision Clarity</p>
			<p class="content-panel__body">Every major move needs a visible owner, context, tradeoff, and next step. I help teams make decisions durable enough to guide the work instead of reopening it.</p>
			<p class="content-panel__eyebrow">02. Visible Momentum</p>
			<p class="content-panel__body">Progress only builds trust when people can see it. I create the rhythms, signals, and communication structures that show what is moving, what is blocked, and what needs attention.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Operating Structures / Capabilities -->
	<div class="section-heading">
		<p class="section-heading__eyebrow">Operating Structures</p>
		<div class="section-heading__line"></div>
		<span class="section-heading__label">Capabilities</span>
	</div>
	<div class="content-grid">
		<article class="content-grid__item">
			<p class="content-grid__label">Alignment Systems</p>
			<h3 class="content-grid__title">Alignment Systems</h3>
			<p class="content-grid__caption">Turning broad goals into shared priorities, stakeholder roles, decision paths, and working rhythms that help complex teams move together.</p>
		</article>
		<article class="content-grid__item">
			<p class="content-grid__label">Project Health Signals</p>
			<h3 class="content-grid__title">Project Health Signals</h3>
			<p class="content-grid__caption">Making risk, dependencies, budget pressure, team strain, and stakeholder confidence visible early enough to act before friction becomes failure.</p>
		</article>
		<article class="content-grid__item">
			<p class="content-grid__label">Launch & Transition Readiness</p>
			<h3 class="content-grid__title">Launch &amp; Transition Readiness</h3>
			<p class="content-grid__caption">Designing the final stretch of complex work with clear criteria, accepted risks, handoff plans, and confidence in what comes next.</p>
		</article>
	</div>

	<!-- Featured Case Study -->
	<FeatureCard
		eyebrow="Featured Case Study"
		title="Launch Confidence Under Pressure"
		description="A compressed launch timeline required clearer decision visibility, sharper triage rhythms, and a shared definition of what was truly launch-critical."
		imageSrc="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1531297484001-80022131f5a1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&q=80"
		imageAlt="Notebook and planning materials on a desk"
		tag="Case Study"
	/>

	<!-- Field Notes -->
	<div class="section-heading">
		<p class="section-heading__eyebrow">Field Notes</p>
		<div class="section-heading__line"></div>
		<span class="section-heading__label">Observations from the space between strategy and execution.</span>
	</div>
	<div class="content-grid">
		<FieldNoteCard
			noteId="Strategy / Field Note"
			quote="When Delivery Becomes Strategic Leadership"
			author="The work between vision and execution deserves a name: operating structure."
			date=""
		/>
		<FieldNoteCard
			noteId="Delivery / Field Note"
			quote="A Project Can Be On Schedule and Still Feel Unsafe"
			author="The first signs of delivery risk often show up as confusion, churn, hesitation, or doubt."
			date=""
		/>
		<FieldNoteCard
			noteId="Operations / Field Note"
			quote="Momentum Is Not Speed"
			author="Progress builds trust when people can see what changed, what matters, and what comes next."
			date=""
		/>
	</div>

	<!-- Closing CTA -->
	<section class="content-panel">
		<header class="content-panel__header">
			<h2 class="content-panel__title">Complex work needs more than a plan.</h2>
			<p class="content-panel__body">It needs aligned stakeholders, visible risks, trusted decisions, and a shared story of what happens next.</p>
		</header>
		<div class="content-panel__content" style="display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;">
			<input
				type="text"
				placeholder="What kind of work needs clarity?"
				style="flex:1;min-width:14rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.62);padding:0.72rem 0.7rem;font:inherit;color:#31271f;"
				aria-label="Describe the kind of work that needs clarity"
			/>
			<InterfaceButton href="/contact" variant="primary">Start a Conversation</InterfaceButton>
		</div>
	</section>
</ShowcaseLayout>
